# File: tests/features/add_greeting_consonant_count_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/213-add-greeting-consonant-count-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Count ASCII consonants in the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Count ASCII consonants in the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_consonant_count is called with Ada and with all 42 ASCII consonants
    Then the results are the Python int values 4 and 45

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Treat y and Y as consonants and ignore every other character
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_consonant_count is called with Ady, Yy, Bob 42!, Émile spelled with precomposed U+00C9, and fullwidth U+FF22 U+FF43 U+FF44
    Then the results are 5, 5, 5, 5, and 3

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_consonant_count is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing existing surfaces
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_consonant_count of Ada, and nmg-smoke Ada runs
    Then the example prints 4 and greeting_consonant_count is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And nmg-smoke prints Hello, Ada with one newline and exit status 0
    And the README documents the 42-letter ASCII consonant set including y and Y, completed-greeting scope, and inherited invalid-name error
